# Start RS Cursor in the background

RS Cursor is the Auto host on port 4331. When it needs to be started or brought back after a crash, use the `AutoSupervise` scheduled task. The task runs `scripts/supervise-hidden.vbs` through `wscript.exe`, so there is no console window. Closing a terminal does not stop the service. Do not point the task at `node.exe` directly — that opens a window, and closing it kills the supervisor.

```powershell
Start-ScheduledTask -TaskName AutoSupervise
```

If the task is missing, install it once with `npm run autostart:install`, then start it the same way.

- Do not run `npm run supervise`, `npm start`, or `node src/server/index.mjs` in a visible terminal.
- Do not host it in an agent background shell either. Those shells are killed with the agent and take the service down.
- If you are inside a live Auto session, restart with `POST /api/restart` so the supervisor brings it back. Do not kill the listener.
- After starting, check `http://127.0.0.1:4331/api/health`.
